 "notes": [
  "Printed: apartment 2, total 60.9 m2; table areas transcribed independently for rooms 1 through 6. The header also identifies floor 11 and apartment example 59.",
  "Measured: scale approximately 57.7 px/m, supported by kitchen 1700 mm across about 98 px, hall 2000 mm across about 115 px, bedroom 2700 mm across about 156 px and 5200 mm across about 300 px. Origin is image pixel (560,304); x right, z down.",
  "Measured: polygons follow inside wall faces and structural projections; kitchen to living and hall to living have open boundaries without invented walls. Door and window openings span the drawn gaps.",
  "Derived: dimensions describe dimension-chain extents, not necessarily rectangular room bounds. Assumed after compiler feedback: kitchen and hall open-space zoning is adjusted to match their printed areas, with complementary changes to the living polygon and no new walls. These zoning boundaries are inferred, not printed physical divisions. The balcony 1600 mm annotation starts below its facade threshold.",
  "Measured: crossed grey kitchen and bathroom service shafts are represented as solid thick wall bands. Hatched central and lower structural projections are retained. Movable furniture is omitted.",
  "Assumed: no photographs supplied; all floor and wall colours, ceiling height 2.7 m, opening heights and window sill heights are placeholders, not observations. Window sill 0.15 m and window height 2.25 m require photographic confirmation.",
  "Measured: kitchen sink, hob, refrigerator symbol, bathroom toilet, shower, basin and lower appliance symbol, and balcony mechanical unit are traced from plan. Assumed: lower bathroom appliance is a washing machine; oven and overhead kitchen cabinets are inferred. Cabinet and fixture vertical dimensions and railing height are assumed.",
  "Derived: compiler-reported wall overhangs, excessive column thickness, kitchen fixture intersections and balcony railing footprints corrected. Structural bands are represented with 0.50 m thickness. No project test/build command or compiler executable is supplied in this output folder; local geometry checks supplement the supplied compiler faults."
